The function is already minimal, so the gain here is small. The rewrite reads `profile` into a local once, which saves the compiler from reloading it. It also marks the error path as unlikely, so the common lookup is laid out as straight-line code. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (idx >= p->numFields), 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numComponents;
}
```